This public consultation is targeting all stakeholders, namely:
•	public authorities responsible for implementation of organic production policy in EU Member States;
•	all relevant EU and national institutions; 
•	stakeholders interested in organic policy such as associations in the agri-food sector, consumer organisations, NGOs and other civil-society organisations representing agricultural, food and environmental issues, at international, EU, national and local level; 
•	research and academic institutions, experts, think-tanks, consultancies;
•	the general public: farmers and other players in the agri-food sector as well as other individuals and organisations wishing to contribute by voicing their opinions as citizens.

consultationObjective:
Through the Farm to Fork and the Biodiversity strategies, published in May 2020, the Commission has committed to: (i) 25% of the EU’s agricultural land being under organic farming by 2030; and (ii) a significant increase in organic aquaculture. These targets aim to both improve the sustainability of the food system and to revert biodiversity loss. To meet this target, the Commission will prepare an action plan to: (i) support the organic sector; (ii) help Member States to stimulate both supply and demand for organic products; and (iii) ensure consumer trust. To inform this action plan, and in line with the Better Regulation principles, the Commission has decided to launch a public consultation to gather stakeholders’ views on challenges and opportunities for the development of organic production and consumption in the EU. The aims of this consultation are: 
•	to give all citizens and organisations the opportunity to be informed about the policy development; 
•	to gather the public’s  opinion on actions to be developed and their possible impacts; 
•	to identify opportunities and challenges for the future of organic production sector in the EU.

